WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:16.432
The Lemonade Detectives hurried back outside.

2
00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:20.182
Henry scanned the crowd, looking for the mysterious woman.

3
00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:25.242
He spotted some shiny green fabric and stepped forward. Then he stopped.

4
00:00:25.243 --> 00:00:27.959
It was just a man wearing a green shirt.

5
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.613
"I don't see her," Cole said.

6
00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:37.091
Henry sighed. "Me neither. It's hard to see anything in this crowd."

7
00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:40.680
"We need to figure out where she went," Maggie declared.

8
00:00:40.681 --> 00:00:43.925
"Because she was definitely acting suspicious!"

9
00:00:43.926 --> 00:00:50.254
"You're right," Cole said. "But why would a stranger steal Nathan's painting?"

10
00:00:50.255 --> 00:00:55.414
Henry was wondering the same thing. "It doesn't make sense," he said.

11
00:00:55.415 --> 00:01:02.055
Maggie frowned. "I told you, that woman is probably an international art thief.

12
00:01:02.056 --> 00:01:05.874
Anyway, why would she run unless she's guilty?"

13
00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:09.168
"I don't know." Henry checked his phone.

14
00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.796
"We only have thirty minutes until the judging starts.

15
00:01:12.797 --> 00:01:16.352
We need to keep investigating all our suspects."

16
00:01:16.353 --> 00:01:20.526
Cole nodded. "We can watch for that woman along the way."

17
00:01:20.527 --> 00:01:25.461
"Let's ask Mrs. Sweet about Mr. Collins' alibi," Henry said.

18
00:01:25.462 --> 00:01:31.130
"After talking with her, we might be able to cross one suspect off the list."

19
00:01:31.131 --> 00:01:35.034
They headed to the crafts fair.

20
00:01:35.035 --> 00:01:40.645
It was easy to spot Mrs. Sweet's booth by the long line near the free candy samples.

21
00:01:40.646 --> 00:01:45.425
"Hi, kids. How's the lemonade business?" Mrs. Sweet asked.

22
00:01:45.426 --> 00:01:47.820
"Great," Maggie said.

23
00:01:47.821 --> 00:01:50.935
"Good!" Mrs. Sweet beamed at them.

24
00:01:50.936 --> 00:01:54.381
"Did you come to sign up for my candy class?

25
00:01:54.383 --> 00:01:58.372
The next one starts right after the art show judging."

26
00:01:58.373 --> 00:02:03.684
"Maybe," Henry said. "Actually, we were wondering something.

27
00:02:03.685 --> 00:02:07.297
Was Mr. Collins here for your last class?"

28
00:02:07.298 --> 00:02:14.830
"Oh yes." Mrs. Sweet chuckled. "I think that man ate more candy than he made!

29
00:02:14.831 --> 00:02:24.904
I had to chase him away after the class ended so I could clean up for the next class."

30
00:02:24.905 --> 00:02:33.544
"Okay, that's one suspect off the list," Cole said as The Lemonade Detectives left the candy booth. "Who's left?"

31
00:02:33.545 --> 00:02:36.127
Maggie ticked them off on her fingers.

32
00:02:36.128 --> 00:02:40.682
"Sunglasses woman, Nora, Hannah, and Patrick."

33
00:02:40.683 --> 00:02:44.460
"Let's try to find Patrick first," Henry said.

34
00:02:44.461 --> 00:02:49.147
"It's kind of suspicious that he didn't meet Owen when he was supposed to."

35
00:02:49.148 --> 00:02:51.666
"True," Cole agreed.

36
00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:57.087
"Maybe he was late because he was busy hiding Nathan's painting in the bushes somewhere."

37
00:02:57.088 --> 00:02:59.693
They headed back toward the art show.

38
00:02:59.694 --> 00:03:04.584
Halfway there they spotted Patrick and Owen standing in line at the burger stand.

39
00:03:04.585 --> 00:03:08.146
"We've been looking for you," Henry told Patrick.

40
00:03:08.147 --> 00:03:13.140
"Join the club." Owen laughed. He didn't seem annoyed anymore.

41
00:03:13.141 --> 00:03:16.819
"You found me," Patrick said. "What's up?"

42
00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:21.750
"Did you hear about Nathan's painting?" Cole asked. "It's missing."

43
00:03:21.751 --> 00:03:26.868
"Yeah, I heard." Patrick didn't look very upset. "So?"

44
00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:30.794
"So where have you been for the past hour?" Maggie blurted out.

45
00:03:30.795 --> 00:03:36.536
Owen laughed again. "Hey, dude," he told Patrick. "They're detectives.

46
00:03:36.537 --> 00:03:38.915
They must think you stole it!"

47
00:03:38.916 --> 00:03:42.850
Patrick's eyes narrowed. "It wasn't me," he said.

48
00:03:42.851 --> 00:03:46.004
"Why would I want a dumb cat painting?

49
00:03:46.005 --> 00:03:49.148
Anyway, I was in the basket-weaving booth.

50
00:03:49.149 --> 00:03:52.052
You can ask Hannah if you don't believe me."

51
00:03:52.053 --> 00:03:58.600
"Okay," Henry said. "Thanks for talking to us." He led Cole and Maggie away.

52
00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:04.364
"Another alibi," Cole said. "I guess we can cross Patrick off the list too."

53
00:04:04.365 --> 00:04:07.234
"I guess so." Henry shrugged.

54
00:04:07.235 --> 00:04:10.800
"We can double-check his alibi when we talk to Hannah."

55
00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:13.631
Soon they reached the basket-weaving booth.

56
00:04:13.632 --> 00:04:16.699
Hannah was arranging baskets on a shelf.

57
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.672
"Hi," Henry said. "We were just talking to Patrick.

58
00:04:20.673 --> 00:04:23.409
He said he was over here earlier."

59
00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.788
"Yeah." Hannah straightened a large blue basket.

60
00:04:26.789 --> 00:04:30.104
"He wanted me to teach him how to weave a basket."

61
00:04:30.105 --> 00:04:35.612
"Really?" Cole asked. "You mean he actually wove one himself?"

62
00:04:35.613 --> 00:04:39.868
Hannah nodded. "He did a pretty good job for a beginner.

63
00:04:39.869 --> 00:04:42.379
You can see for yourself if you want."

64
00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.641
She gestured toward a large shopping bag in the back of the booth.

65
00:04:46.642 --> 00:04:48.944
"His basket is in that bag.

66
00:04:48.945 --> 00:04:53.319
He wanted to leave it here so he wouldn't have to carry it around all day."

67
00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:59.685
"That's okay. We don't need to see it." Henry led the way out of the booth.

68
00:04:59.686 --> 00:05:02.740
"I just realized something," Maggie said.

69
00:05:02.741 --> 00:05:08.470
"Hannah is Patrick's alibi, right? That means Patrick is Hannah's alibi too.

70
00:05:08.471 --> 00:05:11.431
They were together when the painting disappeared."

71
00:05:11.432 --> 00:05:16.182
"So that's two names off the suspect list," Henry said.

72
00:05:16.183 --> 00:05:20.385
"Wait, I just thought of something else." Maggie frowned.

73
00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:23.438
"What if Hannah and Patrick are covering for each other?

74
00:05:23.439 --> 00:05:25.496
They could be in cahoots."

75
00:05:25.497 --> 00:05:30.096
"I doubt it," Cole said. "They don't know each other that well.

76
00:05:30.097 --> 00:05:32.707
They're not even in the same grade."

77
00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:35.619
"You're probably right," Maggie said.

78
00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.056
"I still think the weird woman with the sunglasses did it.

79
00:05:39.057 --> 00:05:41.893
Why else would she run away from us like that?"

80
00:05:41.894 --> 00:05:46.560
Henry bit his lip. "I still don't know what her motive could be.

81
00:05:46.561 --> 00:05:50.086
But I guess she's our only suspect left."

82
00:05:50.087 --> 00:05:54.581
Suddenly he noticed Nora tiptoeing past them, looking rather guilty.

83
00:05:54.582 --> 00:05:58.778
"Well, except for one."
